// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/serve-with-apache.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeServeWithApache(path: "/recipes/serve-with-apache", title: "Serve a site with Apache — Recipes", description: "1.") {
    RecipeShell("Serve a site with Apache", summary: "1. Put this in `public/.htaccess`. The build copies it to the root of `build/`:     ```apache Options -MultiViews RewriteEngine On # A single-page build: # RewriteCond %\{REQUEST_FILENAME\} !-f # RewriteRule ^ /index.html [L] ErrorDocument 404 /404.html Header always set X-Content-Type-Options \"nosniff\" Header always set X-Frame-Options \"DENY\" ```  2. For a single-page build, uncomment the two rewrite lines. 3. Compress the text files. Either turn on `mod_deflate`, which compresses on the way out, or serve the build's `.gz` files with `MultiViews` (in place of `-MultiViews`) and `AddEncoding gzip .gz`. 4. Upload `build/` to the site's document root.  **Verify it:** `curl -I` a page and check for `X-Content-Type-Options` and `X-Frame-Options`. Open a path that does not exist and check that you get the site's `404.html`.", outputs: [], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Build a Docker image", to: "/recipes/docker-image"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Check a deploy", to: "/recipes/check-a-deploy"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Deploy to Cloudflare Pages", to: "/recipes/deploy-to-cloudflare-pages")], source: "md-docs/recipes/serve-with-apache.md", how: false, hasVariations: false) {
    }
}
